---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Terms and Conditions | BitsNotes" 
  description="Read the BitsNotes Terms and Conditions to understand the rules, responsibilities, and limitations that govern your use of our educational platform."
  keywords="bitsnotes terms and conditions, terms of service, educational platform terms, legal terms, DMCA policy"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Terms and Conditions",
      "description": "BitsNotes Terms and Conditions governing use of the educational platform, content usage, and intellectual property.",
      "url": "https://bitsnotes.com/terms"
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16 flex-grow">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-[var(--text)] tracking-tight leading-tight">Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--text-muted)]">Last updated: June 2, 2026. By accessing BitsNotes, you agree to the following terms governing your use of our platform.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--text)] leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>By accessing or using BitsNotes (the "Platform"), you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions and all applicable laws and regulations. If you do not agree with any of these terms, you are prohibited from using or accessing this site. The materials contained in this Platform are protected by applicable copyright and trademark law.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">2. Use of Educational Content</h2>
        <p>BitsNotes provides lecture notes, study guides, and educational materials (collectively, "Content") exclusively for personal, non-commercial educational use. You are permitted to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>View Content within the Platform's viewer for personal study purposes.</li>
          <li>Access materials as an authorised user.</li>
          <li>Use Content to supplement your academic learning and exam preparation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You are expressly prohibited from downloading, reproducing, distributing, publishing, or creating derivative works from any Content without prior written permission from BitsNotes.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">3. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>All Content, design elements, trademarks, and intellectual property on BitsNotes are the exclusive property of BitsNotes or its content providers and are protected by Indian and international copyright and intellectual property laws. Unauthorised use of any materials may violate copyright, trademark, and other applicable laws and could result in legal action.</p>
        <p>The BitsNotes name, logo, and all related product and service names, design marks, and slogans are trademarks of BitsNotes. You may not use these marks without the prior written permission of BitsNotes.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">4. Prohibited Conduct</h2>
        <p>When using BitsNotes, you agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Attempt to circumvent, reverse-engineer, or disable any access-control features on the Platform.</li>
          <li>Use automated tools, bots, scrapers, or scripts to extract or download Content.</li>
          <li>Share, resell, or redistribute any downloaded or screen-captured content from the Platform.</li>
          <li>Impersonate any person or entity or misrepresent your affiliation.</li>
          <li>Upload or transmit viruses or any other type of malicious code.</li>
          <li>Engage in any activity that disrupts or interferes with the Platform's servers or networks.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">5. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>The Content on BitsNotes is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis for educational and informational purposes only. BitsNotes makes no representations or warranties of any kind, express or implied, regarding the accuracy, completeness, reliability, or suitability of the Content for any particular purpose.</p>
        <p>While we strive to keep all lecture notes and study materials accurate and up-to-date, BitsNotes does not guarantee that all Content is error-free. We strongly encourage you to verify important information from official academic sources and your institution's authorised materials.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, BitsNotes and its operators, employees, and affiliates shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your access to or use of (or inability to access or use) the Platform or its Content.</p>
        <p>In no event shall BitsNotes's total liability to you for all damages exceed the amount you have paid BitsNotes in the last six (6) months (which, as BitsNotes is a free service, shall be zero).</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">7. Third-Party Links and Advertisements</h2>
        <p>BitsNotes may display third-party advertisements served by Google AdSense and may contain links to external websites. These third-party sites have separate and independent privacy policies and terms of service. We have no responsibility or liability for the content or activities of these linked sites.</p>
        <p>The inclusion of any link does not imply endorsement by BitsNotes. We encourage you to review the terms and privacy policies of any third-party website you visit.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">8. Content Accuracy and Updates</h2>
        <p>BitsNotes reserves the right to modify, update, or remove any Content at any time without notice. Lecture notes and educational materials may be updated periodically to reflect syllabus changes or corrections. It is your responsibility to check for the most current version of any material before your examinations or assessments.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">9. DMCA and Copyright Complaints</h2>
        <p>If you believe that any Content on BitsNotes infringes upon your copyright, please contact us immediately at <a href="mailto:support@bitsnotes.com" class="text-[var(--accent)] font-bold hover:underline">support@bitsnotes.com</a> with the following information:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>A description of the copyrighted work you claim has been infringed.</li>
          <li>The URL or location of the allegedly infringing material on our Platform.</li>
          <li>Your contact information (name, address, phone number, and email).</li>
          <li>A statement that you have a good faith belief that the use is not authorised by the copyright owner.</li>
          <li>A statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information in your notice is accurate.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We will promptly investigate all valid DMCA notices and take appropriate action, including removal of infringing content where required.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">10. Modifications to Terms</h2>
        <p>BitsNotes reserves the right to revise these Terms and Conditions at any time. We will indicate the date of the last update at the top of this page. By continuing to use the Platform after any changes are posted, you accept and agree to the revised terms. It is your responsibility to review these Terms periodically.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">11. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>These Terms and Conditions shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India, without regard to its conflict of law provisions. Any disputes arising under or in connection with these Terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of India.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-[var(--border)]" />

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-[var(--text)]">12. Contact Information</h2>
        <p>If you have any questions about these Terms and Conditions, please contact us at:</p>
        <div class="border-l-3 border-[var(--accent)] bg-[var(--accent-subtle)] rounded-r-[var(--r-sm)] p-5 text-sm space-y-1">
          <p class="font-bold text-[var(--text)]">BitsNotes Support Team</p>
          <p>Email: <a href="mailto:support@bitsnotes.com" class="text-[var(--accent)] font-bold hover:underline">support@bitsnotes.com</a></p>
          <p>Website: <a href="/" class="text-[var(--accent)] font-bold hover:underline">BitsNotes Platform</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
